WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.280
Speaker 1: Back in early March, at the start of&nbsp;
the Russian invasion of Ukraine, I did a story&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:10.880
called Could Putin be terminally ill? And the&nbsp;
story? It garnered great interest about a quarter&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:16.400
of a million views on YouTube and other similar&nbsp;
number on Facebook. And as I said at the time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:22.720
it was a speculative story. We're trying to make&nbsp;
sense of an invasion that appears to make no&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.720 --> 00:00:30.160
sense. Vladimir Putin's face was pudgy. Could he&nbsp;
be on steroids for some medical condition? Could&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:37.040
it be a reason for rambling and aggression? And&nbsp;
many of you agreed. Yeah, I mean, maybe it is, but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:44.320
it remained quite speculative. There is now much&nbsp;
more pressing speculation about Putin's illness&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.320 --> 00:00:48.880
after a new video of Vladimir Putin has been&nbsp;
released. We have this video, which we're putting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.880 --> 00:00:54.640
up on the screen. This was a meeting that Putin&nbsp;
had with his Defense Minister, Sergei Shoigu.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.640 --> 00:01:00.480
And in the video, Putin is visibly gripping the&nbsp;
table in front of him, apparently for support.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:07.600
He looks pale. He looks bloated, even more&nbsp;
bloated than he previously looked. And he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:13.680
grips the table for basically the entire 12&nbsp;
minute video that was released by the Kremlin.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:22.000
And the idea is that he's gripping it to avoid&nbsp;
some kind of tremor or shaking from being visible.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:25.840
But if he's doing this with his right hand,&nbsp;
if you look at his left hand in the video,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.800 --> 00:01:32.480
it is very shaky and moving around in what&nbsp;
some are describing as a kind of unusual&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.480 --> 00:01:39.040
way. It doesn't seem deliberate. Putin's&nbsp;
kind of hunched back on the seat back,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.040 --> 00:01:44.960
and he's regularly tapping his toes in a way which&nbsp;
it might just be a tick. It could be indicative of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.960 --> 00:01:50.480
something parkinsonian. It could be a side effect&nbsp;
from a medication. Professor Eric Boosie, who's a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.480 --> 00:01:57.960
body language expert from Texas Tech University,&nbsp;
said the face looks clearly bloated and that there&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.960 --> 00:02:05.760
is a general unhealthy appearance. And meanwhile,&nbsp;
the unconfirmed rumors about Putin being in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:11.280
treatment for cancer continued to be published&nbsp;
by various media outlets. They are not confirmed.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.280 --> 00:02:17.680
But it's hard to argue at this point that Putin&nbsp;
seems healthy. Now, the Kremlin has denied&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.680 --> 00:02:24.880
allegations that Putin's health is a problem,&nbsp;
but the speculation has included prostate cancer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.440 --> 00:02:32.800
thyroid cancer, Parkinson's or something.&nbsp;
Parkinsonian tardive dyskinesia is usually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.800 --> 00:02:38.640
a side effect of medication wouldn't tell us&nbsp;
the underlying situation, but it's something&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.640 --> 00:02:44.160
else that's being mentioned now. Why does this&nbsp;
matter? Well, it matters because circumstantially,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.720 --> 00:02:52.640
this relates to the invasion of Ukraine in that if&nbsp;
Putin were very ill, if Putin were terminally ill,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.280 --> 00:03:00.480
it almost would be more sensible that he might be&nbsp;
trying to go out in a blaze of erratic aggression&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:07.120
meant to reconstitute the Soviet Union and being&nbsp;
seen as a martyr for mother Russia. And as crazy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:13.920
as that sounds. It makes more sense than just&nbsp;
like he decided to invade Ukraine, I mean,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:17.840
it makes no sense in in in a&nbsp;
in thinking in a logical way.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.880 --> 00:03:24.800
Now this is one of those, you know, it's a low&nbsp;
probability, but high risk event if this is really&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.800 --> 00:03:32.080
what's going on, if this is an erratic, unhinged&nbsp;
Putin on his last leg as far as his life goes, not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.080 --> 00:03:38.320
his political life. And he thinks, Hey, I'm going&nbsp;
to die soon. What's the downside to using nukes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.960 --> 00:03:45.680
if that's the state of mind that he's in? And&nbsp;
again, this is speculative, but it is fueling the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.680 --> 00:03:51.280
conversation again about. Is anybody thinking of&nbsp;
an assassination attempt? And as I've said before,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:58.000
when we talk about intelligence for&nbsp;
high level Western countries, they are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.640 --> 00:04:05.520
supposed to present all options. And so without&nbsp;
saying anybody's thinking of assassinating Putin,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.240 --> 00:04:10.880
it is without a doubt that when intelligence&nbsp;
had sit down with heads of state,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:11.680 --> 00:04:18.400
they give every option. And so it is almost&nbsp;
a certainty that could it even be done&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.960 --> 00:04:25.120
when it comes to assassinating Putin has been&nbsp;
discussed when we say all options are presented.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.120 --> 00:04:30.240
They present all options. So newfound&nbsp;
questions about Vladimir Putin's health.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.240 --> 00:04:35.360
He doesn't look good. Will we ever really&nbsp;
know the truth? I have absolutely no idea

